Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.21.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.21.0 is a zero-behavior-change infrastructure release: step one of the Swift rewrite. It adds a C bridge surface (Bridge/MFBridge.h/.mm) exposing the frozen ObjC++ hosting core to the future Swift interaction layer - host an app, sync scene geometry, refresh the app list, and a panel-ready query - all forwarding to the exact same code paths as the existing tap-to-host and drag-release flows; closing the panel is honestly stubbed (-2) because the core has no such entry point yet. A Swift facade skeleton (Swift/MFHostBridge.swift) wraps the bridge with Swift error codes and lifecycle event observation via NSNotification; nothing calls it yet. The Makefile compiles Swift for the first time (SWIFT_VERSION 5.0 plus a bridging header) to validate the Theos + roothide + arm64e swiftc toolchain early - the main risk this round. No new config keys, cfgVersion stays 19; runtime behavior is identical to 0.20.0. 0.20.0 fixed the enlarged frozen-picture artifact (corner grip pan swallowing vertical home swipes): the resize handler records the frame at gesture start and, when within 0.8 s the size change is almost purely vertical (dy over 60 pt and dy over 3*dx), rolls the window frame back, disables and re-enables the recognizer, and skips syncContentGeometry so scene.frame is never polluted.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
